	(text "Assumptions to confirm:\n  - r1 is the OBC rail (v1 rail index 0).\n  - These pulls could live on the rail eFuse sheet (#176) instead.\n  - If #176 puts a UVLO divider on each eFuse EN pin, these values need to change."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 228.6 106.68 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "15860b91-17b8-4ff7-adbf-6c609f2e4bd4")
	)
	(text "Channel map (one channel per software rail, from the EPS V2 block diagram):\n  CH0  r1 eFuse (in: 3.3 V)      CH4  r5 eFuse (in: 5 V)\n  CH1  r2 eFuse (in: 3.3 V)      CH5  r6 eFuse (in: Unreg)\n  CH2  r3 eFuse (in: 3.3 V)      CH6  r7 eFuse (in: TBD)\n  CH3  r4 eFuse (in: 3.3 V)      CH7  r8 eFuse (in: TBD)\n\nThe 8 rail eFuses are the same part, so their I2C addresses would collide on one bus.\nDownstream devices must not use 0x70 (the mux's own address).\nI2C_MUX_RST lets firmware clear a stuck channel without a power cycle.\n\nOpen question for Ethan: #122 lists the TPS25947 for the rails, which has no I2C.\nWhich eFuse (or per-rail monitor) sits on these channels, and what addresses can it take?"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 190.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4fed1595-c9cc-4ed3-820b-2c1c331c7f14")
	)
	(text "I2C MUX FOR eFuse TELEMETRY / CONTROL (TCA9548A, address 0x70)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 27.94 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5664b8bb-8b33-4f69-8487-1fbaba85485b")
	)
	(text "RAIL ENABLE BOOT DEFAULTS"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 228.6 27.94 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "87622b23-1404-4109-90d3-300586ae0a4d")
	)
	(text "Channel pull-ups (each channel is its own bus and needs its own pull-ups)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 139.7 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a1f860ab-4126-4b85-8899-296b2e8162d4")
	)
	(text "The MCU drives en x8 directly (block diagram). Its pins float during reset,\nso these set the boot state: r1 (OBC) pulled ON, r2-r8 pulled OFF (EPS boot flow, subsystem_info.md)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 228.6 40.64 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ca26e79b-14af-4953-b485-acaacd94cd5a")
	)
	(text "Upstream pull-ups: drop these if the MCU sheet already has them."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 40.64 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d01c84e5-e676-473f-8b09-c05e24473d9d")
	)
